# `path` for the browser compile: posix only, over the absolute paths of the in-memory snapshot (snapshot-disk.tree).
# Ported from call/code/browser/path.ts, term-cli-in-term-0063. Each task behaves as Node's posix `path` does for an
# absolute input, and every decision is call/code/browser/posix.tree's.
#
# posix.tree is DOCKED (its emitted port), not loaded: loaded, this file's own `join` took the calls posix.tree makes
# to @term/base/list's `join` (type-mismatch at each), a gap in binding by import.
#
# What Node's module shape needs and a Term module cannot say is left to the bundle: `sep` and `delimiter` are tasks
# here, `join` and `resolve` take their paths as one list, and there is no default export or `posix` record.

dock load
  load <@term/call/code/browser/posix>, name posix-port

# `sep`
task read-separator
  like text

  back </>

# `delimiter`
task read-delimiter
  like text

  back <:>

task normalize
  take value, like text
  like text

  back posix-port/normalize(value)

task join
  take paths, like list, like text
  like text

  back posix-port/join-paths(paths)

# the working directory of a worker is the root of the snapshot's filesystem
task resolve
  take paths, like list, like text
  like text

  back posix-port/resolve-paths(paths)

task dirname
  take value, like text
  like text

  back posix-port/dirname(value)

task basename
  take value, like text
  take extension, like text, fall <>
  like text

  back posix-port/basename(value, extension)

task extname
  take value, like text
  like text

  back posix-port/extname(value)

task is-absolute
  take value, like text
  like boolean

  back posix-port/is-absolute(value)

task relative
  take from, like text
  take to, like text
  like text

  back posix-port/relative(from, to)
